   "subject": "Re: MissingPercentage Column",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Hi,<div><br></div><div>Please ignore my earlier message.  I had interpreted your question on the MissingPercentage from the `dataProcess` function&#39;s output, but I realize you were likely referring to the MissingPercentage from the `groupComparison` function.</div><div><br></div><div><div>In that case, missingPercentage is a metric that measures the amount of feature missingness for a protein across all samples.  </div><div><br></div><div>For example, in this table below, there are 6 features that can be measured for a protein, but run 6 only has measurements for 5 of the features.  After performing differential abundance analysis, MSstats will report that the MissingPercentage is 2.78% since out of 36 features that could have been measured across all runs for a protein, only 1 feature is missing.<br></div><div><br></div><div><div>Run     |         Features Measured          |       Total Features</div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;DejaVu Sans&quot;,&quot;Lucida Grande&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Verdana,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:11px\">1 | 6 | 6</span><br></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;DejaVu Sans&quot;,&quot;Lucida Grande&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Verdana,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:11px\">2 </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;DejaVu Sans&quot;,&quot;Lucida Grande&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Verdana,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:11px\">| 6</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;DejaVu Sans&quot;,&quot;Lucida Grande&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Verdana,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:11px\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;DejaVu Sans&quot;,&quot;Lucida Grande&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Verdana,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:11px\">| </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;DejaVu Sans&quot;,&quot;Lucida Grande&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Verdana,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:11px\">6</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font